  <div class="about">
    <div class="about__story">
      <h2 class="display-m" data-split>I was four when my sister handed me my first pack of Magic cards. <em>I have been building doors ever since.</em></h2>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 40px; max-width: 36em;" data-reveal>
        <p>I couldn’t read most of the words yet, but I knew there was a world inside the wrapper, and that the people who made it had left me a door. Everything since traces back to that: competing in card games for fifteen years, coaching players, shipping Skyweaver, running teams at Horizon and Anomaly, and now founding a studio to build a game of my own, end to end.</p>
        <p>I am an engineer by training, a systems designer by temperament, and a competitor by habit. I have led design on a shipped CCG, directed a portfolio of live mobile titles, consulted for CCP Games, Second Dinner and Netflix, and now lead design on an IP-licensed party game at Amber Studio. I work with AI agents daily, for simulation, prototyping and balance, and I believe the best games are fair, deep, and kind to newcomers. The best teams are, too.</p>
        <p>When I am not designing games I am usually playing them, for keeps, at a card table somewhere in Toronto.</p>
      </div>
